# Deployment Safety

## Never

- Deploy uncommitted local changes.
- Force-push `main` without explicit owner approval.
- Modify `docker-compose.prod.yml`, `.env.production`, or run migrations on VPS unless explicitly requested.
- Restart full stack when only `apps/api` changed (backend-only path).

## Git sync (VPS)

Avoid drift between Cursor/local, GitHub `main`, and VPS checkout:

```bash
git fetch origin main:refs/remotes/origin/main
git merge --ff-only origin/main
```

If fast-forward fails, stop and reconcile before building images.

## Standard backend API deploy (VPS)

```bash
docker compose --env-file .env.production -f docker-compose.prod.yml build api
docker compose --env-file .env.production -f docker-compose.prod.yml up -d api
docker compose --env-file .env.production -f docker-compose.prod.yml ps
curl -sS -i http://127.0.0.1:3000/health | head -20
```

After production functional test:

```bash
docker compose --env-file .env.production -f docker-compose.prod.yml logs api --tail 200
```

Full runbook: `docs/ai-context/03_deployment_runbook.md`.

## Post-deploy verification

- Health endpoint returns OK.
- Targeted API test matches expected status (200/429/403), not stale UI cache.
- Logs show expected telemetry for Premium Analysis changes.

## Rollback

- Prefer forward fix on `main`.
- Document deployed commit SHA when reporting production results.
